  "critical": false,
  "description": "Design of electric motors optimized for railway traction: high starting torque, wide speed range, and robustness to shock, dust, and thermal cycling. Covers DC series motors (classic traction motor), AC induction motors with voltage-frequency (V/f) inverter control, and permanent-magnet synchronous machines. Motor cooling, frame mounting (axle-hung vs. body-mounted), and gear reduction are addressed here; fundamental electromagnetism and motor theory are referenced from energy.electricity.motor.",
